The estimated population of DC increased from 678,972 in 2023 to 702,250 in 2024, an increase of 23,278 people, or approximately 3.43%. North Carolina’s estimated population increased from 10,835,491 to 11,046,024, an increase of 210,533 people, or approximately 1.94%. Although North Carolina added more people overall, DC had the larger percentage increase.
Females also represented a slightly larger share of the estimated population in both locations. In 2024, females made up approximately 52.66% of DC’s population and 51.19% of North Carolina’s population. Overall, the results suggest that DC had a younger population and grew at a faster percentage rate, while the age distributions within both locations remained fairly stable between 2023 and 2024. All estimates use PWGTP.

